ly cited contexts by design. Does not establish topical specificity or correct all effects of long bibliographies. It depends on reference scope and support threshold. Order-profile rows are nested and must not be added as independent observations.","reference":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.14355","reference_note":"Background on projection choices; the logarithmic score here is a custom exploratory choice, not the cited paper’s metric."},"deduplication":{"version":1,"policy":"Conservative title-and-author matching; long-title typo tolerance is two character edits. Books may combine recorded years. Conflicting article DOIs stay separate except matching JSTOR / Academy of Management aliases. Reviews, unknown publication types, conflicting authors, materially different titles and unresolved IDs stay separate without a shared DOI. Counts use distinct canonical source works.","originalSources":2855,"sources":2855,"mergedGroups":[{"canonicalId":"https://openalex.org/W2134049139","years":[1977],"records":[{"id":"https://openalex.org/W2134049139","title":"Self-efficacy: Toward a unifying theory of behavioral change.","year":1977,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1037//0033-295x.84.2.191"},{"id":"https://openalex.org/W4292808503","title":"Self-efficacy: Toward a unifying theory of behavioral change.","year":1977,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1037/0033-295x.84.2.191"}],"reason":"Same DOI"},{"canonicalId":"https://openalex.org/W2126186544","years":[1984],"records":[{"id":"https://openalex.org/W2126186544","title":"Upper Echelons: The Organization as a Reflection of Its Top Managers","year":1984,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.5465/amr.1984.4277628"},{"id":"https://openalex.org/W3121736426","title":"Upper Echelons: The Organization as a Reflection of Its Top Managers","year":1984,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.2307/258434"}],"reason":"Matching title, authors and years across JSTOR / Academy of Management DOI aliases"},{"canonicalId":"https://openalex.org/W2141951329","years":[1989],"records":[{"id":"ht